From e934146bf153897eca01404584ba969aa639647e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:59:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 055/240] Bugfix: rebase load arrays and halo end array in
 `meshBase()` and `hmeshBase()` [report R. Perry]

`meshBase()` did not shift the `velotax` and `vnlotax` array accesses,
so after a base change the load arrays were read at the wrong offset
(`meshCheck()` reports invalid loads). `hmeshBase()` looped over the
new element range while `vehdtax` was still based on the old one, and
when `vehdtax` aliased `m.vendtax` it added the adjustment a second
time to entries that `meshBase()` had just rebased.

Shift the load arrays like `graphBase()` does. In `hmeshBase()`, re-
alias `vehdtax` when it is the mesh end array, else rebase the array
access before updating its entries.

Add `test_mesh_base`, which rebases a loaded mesh and a halo mesh (with
aliased and with distinct halo end arrays) back and forth and checks
them.

Refs: SEP-23
